        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3ca15bcb-7d4c-582d-a2f7-9b5036ce0df8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: 41st Tactical Squadron, 41st Air Tactical Squadron, 22nd Air Base, German Luftwaffe, Eighth Air Force\n- Products: Mikoyan MiG-29, Sukhoi Su-27, McDonnell Douglas F-15 Eagle, General Dynamics F-16 Fighting Falcon\n- Companies: Mikoyan design bureau\n- Places: Marienburg, Anklam, Gdynia, Poland, Nazi Germany, Soviet Union\n- Concepts: air superiority fighter\n- Events: October 1943 attacks\n\nFacts:\n- In October 1943, Eighth Air Force attacks targeted industrial sites in Nazi Germany at Anklam, the 22nd Air Base in Marienburg on the 9th, and Gdynia in occupied Poland.\n- During the 1970s, the Mikoyan design bureau developed the Mikoyan MiG-29 in the Soviet Union as an air superiority fighter.\n- The Mikoyan MiG-29 was developed alongside the larger Sukhoi Su-27 to counter the McDonnell Douglas F-15 Eagle and the General Dynamics F-16 Fighting Falcon.\n- The Mikoyan MiG-29 is a twin-engine jet fighter aircraft.\n- The 41st Tactical Squadron operates Mikoyan MiG-29 jet fighters acquired from the German Luftwaffe.\n- The main unit based at the 22nd Air Base is the 41st Air Tactical Squadron, which flies Mikoyan MiG-29 fighters.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "757496aa-e0e9-51a1-b28e-6fd9d4dba851",
        "text": "Page: 41st Tactical Squadron. Sentence: 41st Tactical Squadron (known as 41.\nPage: 41st Tactical Squadron. Sentence: The squadron operates Mikoyan MiG-29 jet fighters acquired from the German Luftwaffe.\nPage: Mikoyan MiG-29. Sentence: The Mikoyan MiG-29 (Russian: Микоян МиГ-29 ; NATO reporting name: Fulcrum) is a twin-engine jet fighter aircraft designed in the Soviet Union.\nPage: Mikoyan MiG-29. Sentence: Developed by the Mikoyan design bureau as an air superiority fighter during the 1970s, the MiG-29, along with the larger Sukhoi Su-27, was developed to counter new American fighters such as the McDonnell Douglas F-15 Eagle, and the General Dynamics F-16 Fighting Falcon.\nPage: 22nd Air Base. Sentence: The main unit based there is the 41st Air Tactical Squadron flying MiG-29 fighters.\nPage: Target for Today. Sentence: The October 1943 footage was filmed during Eighth Air Force attacks on Nazi Germany industrial targets in Anklam, the 22nd Air Base in Marienburg (on the 9th), and Gdynia in occupied Poland.",
